+---
+id: dl-004-apply-json-merge-patch-immutably-with-json-value-validation
+type: decision-log
+title: "Apply JSON Merge Patch immutably with JSON-value validation"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 7386 defines merge behavior for JSON documents, while this library receives JavaScript values
+and its existing patch API guarantees that a supplied document is never changed.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate both `applyMergePatch` arguments using the existing JSON-value validation rules, and build
+the result by cloning values as they are merged. Use own data properties and `defineProperty` for
+object writes so keys such as `__proto__` remain JSON data rather than prototype mutations.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Merge Patch has standards-defined behavior for JSON data only, returns an independent result, and
+does not introduce JavaScript prototype semantics into JSON object processing.
